---
title: Umbra Authentication Flow
---
sequenceDiagram
  participant B as Web Browser
  participant S as Umbra Server
  participant DB as Database

  rect rgb(200, 220, 255)
    Note over B,DB: Signing In
    B->>S: Submit username and password to /api/auth/login/
    Note right of S: Rate-limited to 5 attempts per minute to block brute-force attacks
    S->>DB: Check credentials against stored (hashed) password
    DB-->>S: User account found or not found
    alt Credentials are correct
      S->>S: Create a session record in the database
      S->>S: Generate a CSRF token
      S-->>B: Success response + two cookies set by the browser automatically
      Note left of B: sessionid cookie (HttpOnly)
      Note left of B: Proves your identity on every request
      Note left of B: Cannot be read by JavaScript for security
      Note left of B: csrftoken cookie (readable by JS)
      Note left of B: App reads this value and sends it as a header
      Note left of B: Prevents cross-site request forgery attacks
    else Wrong username or password
      S-->>B: 401 Unauthorized
    end
  end

  rect rgb(200, 255, 200)
    Note over B,DB: Making an Authenticated Request
    B->>S: API request + sessionid cookie + X-CSRFToken header
    Note right of S: The server performs two security checks
    Note right of S: 1. Looks up the session to identify the user
    Note right of S: 2. Validates the CSRF token to confirm the request
    Note right of S: came from your app, not a malicious third-party site
    S->>DB: Look up session and fetch requested data
    DB-->>S: Session valid, data returned
    S-->>B: JSON response
  end

  rect rgb(255, 240, 200)
    Note over B,DB: Signing Out
    B->>S: POST /api/auth/logout/
    Note right of S: Accepts the request even if the session has already expired
    Note right of S: This prevents a confusing error when logging out of a stale session
    S->>DB: Delete the session record from the database
    S-->>B: 204 No Content (signed out successfully)
    Note left of B: App clears the signed-in user state
    Note left of B: and redirects to the login page
  end
